From fd8c5e83632ad5f0ac3c94fa4b603e86384e45f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moises Santana <191926848+msantana-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:34:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] platform: name the host after the cartridge and give the
 settings menu shape

Seven changes to the SDL host. None of them reach the guest framebuffer, which
is what keeps the oracle comparisons meaningful - frame dumps at frames 400, 700,
1000, 1100 and 1200 are byte-identical to a build from before any of this, and
the gates are unchanged at 75/75, SameBoy 3 EXACT + 2 NEAR 0.004, PyBoy 5/5.

The window and the settings menu both opened as "GameBoy Recompiled", the
upstream engine's own product name, applied to every ROM the user supplies.
gbrt_get_rom_title() already existed and was only naming the save file; it is
now exported and reads the cartridge header at 0x134.

The menu had controls spanning the whole window - a 1900 px "Speed %" slider on
a 4K display - with each label stranded against the far edge because widgets
carry their label as their last argument. The content is now bounded and
centred, sections got a rule and the accent colour, and the default Dear ImGui
blue gave way to the greens of a DMG palette.

Host actions had no feedback at all: fast forward, save/load state, state slot
and mute all changed state silently. They now confirm in a bottom-right toast
for 1.5 s. It is a sibling if rather than another else if, because the menu and
the debug overlay are mutually exclusive and a toast in that chain would vanish
exactly when the player opens the menu.

The audio section no longer dumps ring buffer occupancy and device buffer
geometry into the settings flow as if they were options; those moved to the
debug overlay, which already reported ring fill and underruns.
